\b Google Ads API Design Documentation\b0\par
\par
\b Company / Product\b0\par
Tiresias View is a SaaS platform for document-based scenario analysis and simulation. Users upload reports and source materials, and the system helps analyze stakeholder reactions, market scenarios, and public-opinion outcomes.\par
\par
\b Purpose of Google Ads API Usage\b0\par
We use the Google Ads API only for our own first-party marketing operations for Tiresias View. The API is not used for a third-party advertising platform, reseller product, or arbitrage business.\par
\par
\b Intended Use Cases\b0\par
1. Create and manage Google Search campaigns for Tiresias View.\par
2. Create and update ad groups, keywords, negative keywords, and responsive search ads.\par
3. Retrieve campaign performance reports and search term reports for internal optimization.\par
4. Track and upload conversions related to our own service, including sign-ups, quote requests, and completed purchases.\par
\par
\b Users and Access Model\b0\par
The tool is used internally by our company only. Access is limited to authorized operators managing the Tiresias View Google Ads account. OAuth credentials and API credentials are stored securely and are not exposed to end users.\par
\par
\b Data Flow\b0\par
1. An authorized operator configures Google Ads API credentials.\par
2. Internal scripts call the Google Ads API to create or update campaigns and retrieve reports.\par
3. Conversion events from our own product flows are recorded and, where appropriate, uploaded to Google Ads for attribution.\par
4. Retrieved reporting data is used only for internal campaign optimization.\par
\par
\b Compliance Statement\b0\par
We use the API only to manage and measure ads for our own business. We do not provide a public ad management product, do not resell Google Ads data, and do not share API data with unauthorized third parties.\par
\par
\b Primary Website\b0\par
https://tiresiasview.com\par
